@page
@model FixITCity_Dashboard.Pages.PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    Layout = "_SidebarLayout";
}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/privacy.css" />
<div class="privacy-container">
    <div class="privacy-header">
        <h2>Privacy Policy & Data Governance</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-card">
        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> 1. Introduction</h3>
            <p>
                Welcome to <strong>FixITCity</strong>. We are committed to protecting your personal information and respecting your privacy. 
                This Privacy Policy explains how our municipal service portal collects, uses, discloses, and safeguards your information when 
                you use our dashboard and fault-reporting platform.
            </p>
            <p>
                We process personal information in accordance with applicable data protection legislation, including the 
                <strong>Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA)</strong>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-database"></i> 2. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p>To effectively manage and track municipal infrastructure faults, we collect the following categories of information:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account Details:</strong> Your full name, email address, and administrative role assigned by municipal management.</li>
                <li><strong>Fault Report Data:</strong> Descriptions, categories, and timestamps of reported municipal issues.</li>
                <li><strong>Media & Photos:</strong> Images uploaded by citizens or administrators depicting infrastructure faults.</li>
                <li><strong>Geospatial Data:</strong> GPS coordinates and address lines automatically attached to fault reports to assist maintenance field teams.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-map-marked-alt"></i> 3. Use of Location & Media</h3>
            <p>
                GPS coordinates and submitted photographs are utilized exclusively for locating, verifying, and resolving municipal service disruptions 
                (such as potholes, water leaks, or street light outages). Location data is not tracked continuously or used for unauthorized surveillance.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-lock"></i> 4. Data Security & Storage</h3>
            <p>
                We implement robust administrative, technical, and physical security measures—including encrypted database storage and secure cloud repositories (such as Supabase)—to 
                protect your personal data against unauthorized access, accidental loss, or unlawful alteration.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> 5. Your Rights Under POPIA</h3>
            <p>You have the legal right to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you.</li>
                <li>Request correction or deletion of inaccurate or outdated information.</li>
                <li>Object to the processing of your personal information under specific circumstances.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-section">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-envelope-open-text"></i> 6. Contact Information</h3>
            <p>
                If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact our Information Officer:
            </p>
            <div class="contact-box">
                <p><strong>Municipal Information Officer</strong></p>
                <p><i class="fas fa-envelope"></i> privacy@fixitcity.gov.za</p>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4 text-center">
        <a asp-page="/Index" class="btn btn-secondary">
            <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Dashboard
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
